@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="space-y-6">
    <section class="rounded-[2rem] border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8 lg:p-10">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-stone-500">Legal and privacy</p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-4xl text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-stone-900 sm:text-4xl">
            Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-7 text-stone-600 sm:text-base">
            This page explains what information Megdan collects, how it is used during complaint submission and tracking,
            and how the platform protects personal information while supporting communication between citizens and local authorities.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
            <div class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-4">
                <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-stone-500">Submission model</p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium text-stone-900">Guest complaint submission</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-4">
                <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-stone-500">Main contact data</p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium text-stone-900">Email-based tracking and updates</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-4">
                <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-stone-500">Public visibility</p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium text-stone-900">Personal data hidden from public map views</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr]">
        <aside class="rounded-[2rem] border border-stone-200 bg-stone-900 p-6 text-white shadow-sm sm:p-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-stone-400">At a glance</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">How Megdan handles your complaint data</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-stone-300">
                The platform is designed to help citizens report issues, allow administrators to review and resolve them,
                and use AI support to improve categorization, prioritization, and duplicate detection.
            </p>

            <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
                <div class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-4">
                    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">We collect only data needed for complaint handling</p>
                    <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-300">
                        This includes complaint details, contact email, location data, and any optional files you upload.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-4">
                    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">Public complaint views must not expose personal identity</p>
                    <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-300">
                        Public or map-based complaint displays should show complaint information without exposing private personal contact data.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-brand-400/20 bg-brand-500/10 p-4">
                    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-brand-200">Important note</p>
                    <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-200">
                        Access links sent by email should be treated as private, because they may allow access to complaint tracking pages without a citizen account.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </aside>

        <div class="space-y-6">
            <section class="rounded-[2rem] border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900">1. Information we collect</h2>
                <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-stone-600 sm:text-base">
                    <p>
                        When you submit a complaint, Megdan may collect the complaint title, detailed description, your email address,
                        the location of the issue, and any address details you provide.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        If image upload is enabled, the system may also store complaint-related images in supported formats such as JPG or PNG,
                        together with references linking those files to the complaint record.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The system may also store operational information such as complaint status, AI-generated category or priority suggestions,
                        tracking tokens, notification logs, administrator actions, timestamps, and optional feedback submitted after resolution.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="rounded-[2rem] border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900">2. How your data is used</h2>
                <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-stone-600 sm:text-base">
                    <p>
                        Megdan uses submitted information to register a complaint, allow administrators to review it,
                        assign or confirm categories and priority levels, and track progress from submission to resolution.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Your email address is used for complaint-related communication, including status updates,
                        secure tracking links, and other service notifications connected to your complaint.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Location data is used to place the complaint on a map, support municipal review,
                        and enable public or admin-side complaint map views while keeping personal identity hidden from public displays.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="rounded-[2rem] border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900">3. AI-assisted processing</h2>
                <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-stone-600 sm:text-base">
                    <p>
                        Megdan includes AI-assisted features that may classify complaints, estimate urgency or priority,
                        analyse frustration level, and suggest similar complaints to reduce duplicate reporting.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        These automated results are intended to support complaint handling and administrative review,
                        but they should not be treated as the sole basis for important decisions without human oversight.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        If the AI is unavailable or unable to classify a complaint correctly, the system should provide clear feedback
                        and allow the complaint workflow to continue with appropriate review handling.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="rounded-[2rem] border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900">4. Guest tracking and access links</h2>
                <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-stone-600 sm:text-base">
                    <p>
                        Citizens submit complaints in guest mode and do not need to create a public user account in order to file or track a complaint.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Instead, the platform may issue a secure token-based tracking link or access link by email so that you can review complaint progress
                        and access complaint-related updates.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        You are responsible for keeping those links private. Anyone with the link may potentially access the related tracking page,
                        depending on how the application is configured.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="rounded-[2rem] border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900">5. Sharing and visibility</h2>
                <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-stone-600 sm:text-base">
                    <p>
                        Complaint data is primarily processed within the Megdan platform by authorized administrators responsible for complaint review and resolution.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Certain information may also be processed by supporting services such as map providers,
                        CAPTCHA providers, email delivery services, or hosting infrastructure used to operate the application.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Public map views and similar public-facing pages should display complaint information without exposing personal user data such as email address or name.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="rounded-[2rem] border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900">6. Retention, security, and logging</h2>
                <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-stone-600 sm:text-base">
                    <p>
                        Complaint records, notification logs, uploaded files, and related administrative history may be retained for operational, reporting,
                        quality assurance, and audit purposes, depending on project or deployment settings.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The system should apply reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect stored data,
                        including access control for admin functions, secure handling of tracking mechanisms, and validation of uploaded files.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The application may also log which authority member changed a complaint status and when that change occurred,
                        in order to support accountability and traceability.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="rounded-[2rem] border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900">7. Your choices</h2>
                <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-stone-600 sm:text-base">
                    <p>
                        You may choose how much detail to include in a complaint, but enough information should be provided to allow proper review and resolution.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Image uploads and post-resolution feedback may be optional, depending on the specific complaint flow enabled in the application.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Because Megdan is designed for complaint handling, removing or changing certain submitted information may not always be possible after a complaint has been filed.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="rounded-[2rem] border border-stone-200 bg-brand-50 p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900">Contact and updates</h2>
                <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-stone-700 sm:text-base">
                    This privacy policy should be reviewed and adapted further before production deployment so that it matches the exact hosting setup,
                    third-party services, retention periods, and legal obligations that apply to your real deployment environment.
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>